{"id": "unknown-2026-09-30-006", "date": "2026-09-30", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 40, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["cotton_price", "supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.67, "keywords": ["decline", "weak", "pressure"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India polyester, PC yarn soften; viscose market shows mixed trend", "content": "India’s man-made yarn markets showed a mixed-to-weaker trend as sluggish demand, payment constraints and inventory pressure affected buying.\nPolyester and speciality yarn prices declined in Surat, while polyester yarn stayed steady in Ludhiana and PC yarn eased.\nViscose rose in Surat after production cuts reduced supply, while Mumbai was stable; north Indian cotton fell by ₹400 (~$4.16) per maund.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-polyester-pc-yarn-soften-viscose-market-shows-mixed-trend-313875-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
